.TH SET_GIT_ENV.SH 1 "2026-09-14" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
set_git_env.sh \- configure git and GitHub access from the Kerberos principal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B source set_git_env.sh
[\fB\-k\fR \fIkey\fR]
[\fB\-l\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B set_git_env.sh
derives the git identity and GitHub credentials of the current operator
from \fBKRB5_PRINCIPAL\fR, which
.BR get_krb_principal.sh (1)
exports. It:
.IP \(bu 4
sets git \fBuser.email\fR to the full principal and \fBuser.name\fR to
the part before the \fB@\fR;
.IP \(bu 4
exports \fBGIT_SSH_COMMAND\fR pointing at the per-user key
\fI~/.ssh/id_<user>_rsa\fR;
.IP \(bu 4
adds that key to the ssh-agent \(em but only when stdin is a terminal,
so there is somewhere to type the passphrase, and only when an agent
exists to hold it. A key whose fingerprint is already loaded is not
added again, so the passphrase is not requested twice.
.PP
Each step reports \fBPass\fR in green or \fBFail\fR in red. A missing
private key is a \fBFail\fR on the SSH step but does not stop the rest.
.PP
Because the identity comes from the ticket rather than from a hardcoded
table, one set of dotfiles serves every shifter, and commits made from
a shared group account are still attributed to the individual.
.PP
.B This script should be sourced,
so \fBGIT_SSH_COMMAND\fR persists.
.SH OPTIONS
Configuration precedence is command line, then environment variable,
then .env file, then built-in default.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " " \fIFILE\fR
Private key for \fBGIT_SSH_COMMAND\fR. Environment:
\fBGIT_SSH_KEY\fR. Default: \fI~/.ssh/id_<user>_rsa\fR, where
\fI<user>\fR is the principal's user part.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-local
Write the identity to the repository's config (\fB\-\-local\fR) instead
of the user's global config. Useful when only one clone should carry
this identity.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print the resolved settings and the full \fBssh\-add\fR output.
Environment: \fBVERBOSE\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and return.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KRB5_PRINCIPAL
Required input. Without it the script reports a \fBFail\fR and returns
1.
.TP
.B GIT_SSH_COMMAND
Exported by this script.
.TP
.B SSH_AUTH_SOCK
Consulted to decide whether an agent is available.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 1 when \fBKRB5_PRINCIPAL\fR is unset, and 2 for
an unrecognised option.
.SH EXAMPLES
Configure this shell for GitHub access:
.PP
.RS
.nf
source get_krb_principal.sh
source set_git_env.sh -v
.fi
.RE
.PP
Apply the identity only to the current clone:
.PP
.RS
.nf
source set_git_env.sh --local
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR get_krb_principal.sh (1),
.BR get_krb_daq_principal.sh (1),
.BR setup-online.sh (1),
.BR git-config (1),
.BR ssh-add (1)
